      <h2>Gold Mining Equipment for Suriname</h2>
      <p>Suriname's gold sector is one of the most active in South America relative to country size, with significant alluvial production from the Brokopondo, Sipaliwini, and Marowijne districts. Most operations are small and medium-scale (ASM), working the rich placer ground of the Guiana Shield greenstone belt. Our wash plants are container-ready for Paramaribo and engineered for the heavy clay, rainforest humidity, and remote-camp conditions Surinamese miners face every day.</p>
      <h3>Why Surinamese Miners Choose Us</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Container-ready for shipping into Paramaribo with riverine onward logistics</li>
        <li>Mercury-free — supports compliance with Minamata Convention and Surinamese ASGM regulations</li>
        <li>Built for Guiana Shield greenstone laterite and heavy clay alluvials</li>
        <li>Handles tropical rainfall, high humidity, and seasonal river flow</li>
        <li>Simple operation suited to ASM crews and family-scale operators</li>
        <li>30-minute setup means more productive hours in short dry-season windows</li>
      </ul>
      <p>From the rich Brokopondo placer ground to the remote camps in Sipaliwini, our equipment recovers fine gold that hand sluices and shaker tables routinely miss. <a href="/contact/">Contact us for Suriname pricing and shipping quotes</a>.</p>
